{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>In the thickness of the cloud.</b> The Ramban wrote: this is the fog (ערפל) which Elohim placed there, and all see and recognize it, as it says, ״ומראה כבוד ה' כאש אוכלת״ and so forth. And Scripture says, ״הנה אנכי בא אליך בעב הענן״ — that you would approach into the fog, so that the people would hear My words and they themselves would be prophets through My words — not that they would believe from the mouth of others; as it says (Deuteronomy 4:10), saying, HaShem said to me, Assemble Me the people and I will make them hear My words, that they may learn to fear Me all the days, and so forth. And through you they will believe forever in all generations, and if a prophet or a dreamer of dreams arises among them against your words, they will immediately deny him, for they already saw with their own eyes and heard with their own ears that you attained the highest level of prophecy. It will be made clear to them from you what is written (Numbers 12:6–7): ״אם יהיה נביאכם ה' במראה אליו אתודע בחלום אדבר בו לא כן עבדי משה״ and so forth, ״פה אל פה אדבר בו״. Therefore it says, ״בעבור ישמע העם בדברי עמך״, for they would hear My words from within the fire and know that I am HaShem speaking with you, and they would believe in My words and also believe in you forever. And likewise what they said — ״היום הזה ראינו כי ידבר אלהים את האדם וחי״ — is to say: Behold, the divine speech has been fulfilled among us by the seeing of our eyes, as was the will of Elohim; and from now on, you approach, so that we may know concerning you that you attained the highest level above all the prophets."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:06.690543343Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}